// XBRAIN_V6 realtime-plane Zenoh router configuration.
//
// See 11 S1.1.2:
//   * mode: router
//   * realtime-plane endpoint: tcp/127.0.0.1:7449 (loopback ONLY)
//   * scouting: multicast OFF (RT-C1); gossip ON with multihop OFF
//     (RT-C2 as corrected 2026-08-23) -- the RT plane MUST NOT
//     auto-discover the general plane, and what guarantees that is
//     MULTICAST being off plus multihop being false, NOT gossip
//     being off.
//
//     Corrected 2026-09-17 (CLAUDE.md iron rule 1). These three lines
//     used to read "multicast + gossip DISABLED ... both scouting
//     mechanisms are hard-off", which CONTRADICTED THE BODY OF THIS
//     VERY FILE a few lines below, where gossip is enabled with the
//     measurement that forced it. A header that disagrees with its own
//     config is worse than no header: it is the part people read.
//
// The RT plane is a 20 Hz safety-critical control loop and MUST stay
// on-host. The tcp/127.0.0.1 bind guarantees no packet leaves the
// ORIN loopback interface (RT-C4 assumption).
//
// This config is loaded by scripts/dev/start_voice_loop.sh via
//   zenohd --config configs/zenoh/router_rt.json5
// 2026-08-10 (V-ORIN-ZN-GOSSIP): gossip enabled on the ROUTER side.
//
// The peer-session <-> router setup requires SOMEONE to propagate
// subscription/publisher declarations between peers, so a subscriber
// on one peer can be reached by a publisher on another. When BOTH
// router and sessions had gossip=false, the router accepted every
// peer's TCP connection but never forwarded declarations, so
// pub.put() vanished (verified via two-session probe 2026-08-10:
// mode=peer/gossip=off -> 0 rx; mode=client -> 3 rx).
//
// The RT-C1/C2 rule "RT plane MUST NOT auto-discover the general
// plane" is preserved by:
//   * multicast STILL disabled (no beacon frames)
//   * gossip enabled ONLY inside this router's connected peer set,
//     which is scoped to loopback tcp:7449 -- the RT router does
//     not connect to any other router, so its gossip domain is
//     exactly the RT-plane processes and nothing else.
//
// Sessions themselves ALSO enable gossip, for the same reason
// (xbrain/common/zenoh/session_factory.py REQUIRES enabled=True;
// grep 'gossip_cfg.get("enabled") is not True').
//
// Corrected 2026-09-17 (CLAUDE.md iron rule 1). This line used to say
// "Sessions themselves keep gossip disabled", which was simply false
// and pointed at the file that proves it false. Both ends of the link
// need gossip on: the router forwards declarations, and a session with
// gossip off never sends its own subscription table to be forwarded.
{
  mode: "router",
  listen: {
    endpoints: [
      "tcp/127.0.0.1:7449",
    ],
  },
  scouting: {
    multicast: {
      enabled: false,
    },
    gossip: {
      enabled: true,
      multihop: false,
    },
  },
}
